You have left this choice open, and each option gives a different result:
- "co-expression adjusted for the covariates": COBRA gives the part of each gene pair's co-expression associated with each covariate in a design matrix (e.g. group, batch), and a covariate-adjusted co-expression matrix.
- "separate co-expression network per patient": LIONESS-COEXPRESSION gives one gene-gene co-expression network per sample, plus the aggregate; BONOBO gives one gene-gene co-expression network per sample, estimated with a Bayesian model; optionally per-edge p-values per sample.

